<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen stable.</title>
<headline>Pakistani yarn rates end steady, seen stable.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton yarn rates closed steady on Wednesday and dealers predicted that prices would remain stable amid steady conditions in the domestic cotton market.</p>
<p>Rates in rupee supplied by the Pakistan Yarn Merchant Association for a 10-lb (4.5-kg) cone of 21 counts:</p>
<p>    Al-Karam (A.K.)	    490	    490</p>
<p>    Shafiq (Gold ky.)	  465	    465</p>
<p>    M.G.M.			 490	    490</p>
<p>    ($1 = 40.22 rupees)    -- Ovais Subhani 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
